./ R 00173000 00175000 $ 00173100 100                                           
*  S/370 ONLY -- NO ESA/390 COUNTERPART.  RENAMED, NOT         XA0001DK         
*  DELETED, SO A SURVIVING REFERENCE FAILS TO ASSEMBLE         XA0001DK         
*  RATHER THAN READ LOWCORE THAT NOW MEANS SOMETHING ELSE.     XA0001DK         
*  STIDC IS GONE, AND THE CHANNEL SUBSYSTEM REPLACES           XA0001DK         
*  CHANNEL LOGOUT WITH THE ESW AND ERW IN THE IRB PLUS         XA0001DK         
*  STCRW.  DELETING THEM WOULD LEAVE NO TRACE OF A             XA0001DK         
*  DECISION A 64-BIT PASS HAS TO MAKE AGAIN.  EXPECTED TO      XA0001DK         
*  BREAK DMKIOG DMKPRV DMKCCH DMKEIG -- ALL CHANNEL-ERROR      XA0001DK         
*  AND STIDC-SIMULATION PATHS.  SEE RISK R-03.                 XA0001DK         
S370CHID DS    1F -           STIDC CHANNEL ID, S/370          XA0001DK         
S370IOEL DS    1F -           IO EXTENDED LOGOUT PTR, S/370    XA0001DK         
S370ECSW DS    1F -           LIMITED CHANNEL LOGOUT, S/370    XA0001DK         
./ R 00175100          $ 00175110 010                                           
         ORG   S370ECSW                                        XA0001DK         
./ R 00175300          $ 00175310 010                                           
S370EBY3 DS    1X             3RD BYTE OF LCL, S/370           XA0001DK         
./ R 00177000 00178000 $ 00177100 010                                           
*  X'B8' IS THE ESA/390 SUBSYSTEM-IDENTIFICATION WORD,         XA0001DK         
*  X'BC' THE INTERRUPTION PARAMETER.  CP'S INTKFLIN            XA0001DK         
*  ALREADY SAT ON THAT EXACT FULLWORD, AND ITS LOW             XA0001DK         
*  HALFWORD IS THE SUBCHANNEL NUMBER, BECAUSE THE              XA0001DK         
*  SUBSYSTEM ID IS X'0001' IN THE HIGH HALFWORD.  SO           XA0001DK         
*  NOTHING MOVES AND NOTHING CHANGES WIDTH; ONLY THE           XA0001DK         
*  MEANING DOES.  MEASURED IN 07-io-interrupt.rc, WHICH        XA0001DK         
*  READ X'B8' FOR FOUR BYTES AND MATCHED 00010000.             XA0001DK         
*                                                              XA0001DK         
*  INTTIO IS RENAMED WITH NO ALIAS, DELIBERATELY.  19 OF       XA0001DK         
*  ITS 21 REFERENCES COMPARE IT AGAINST A DEVICE ADDRESS       XA0001DK         
*  -- WHICH A SUBCHANNEL NUMBER IS NOT -- SO AN ALIAS          XA0001DK         
*  WOULD LET EVERY ONE KEEP ASSEMBLING AND SILENTLY            XA0001DK         
*  COMPARE THE WRONG THING.  THAT IS RISK R-02, THE JOINT      XA0001DK         
*  TOP RISK, AND THIS IS THE CHEAPEST PLACE TO MAKE IT         XA0001DK         
*  LOUD.                                                       XA0001DK         
*                                                              XA0001DK         
*  THESE OFFSETS ARE UNCHANGED IN Z/ARCHITECTURE, SO THE       XA0001DK         
*  NAMES BELOW CARRY FORWARD WITHOUT EDIT.                     XA0001DK         
IOSSID   DS    1F -           ESA/390 SUBSYSTEM ID WORD        XA0001DK         
INTKFLIN EQU   IOSSID -       S/370 NAME, SAME FULLWORD        XA0001DK         
IOSCHNO  EQU   IOSSID+2 -     ESA/390 SUBCHANNEL NUMBER        XA0001DK         
*                                                              XA0001DK         
*  AND A GUEST'S PAGE 0 IS NOT CP'S LOWCORE.  PSA SERVES       XA0001DK         
*  BOTH: CP'S OWN REAL LOWCORE, AND A TEMPLATE FOR A           XA0001DK         
*  VIRTUAL MACHINE'S PAGE 0 -- EVERY  X-PSA(,R2)  SITE.        XA0001DK         
*  GUESTS STAY S/370-MODE THROUGH M4, SO A GUEST-PSA           XA0001DK         
*  DISPLACEMENT KEEPS ITS S/370 MEANING.  DMKDSP BUILDS A      XA0001DK         
*  GUEST INTERRUPT CODE HERE FROM VDEVADD+VCUADD+VCHADD, A     XA0001DK         
*  VIRTUAL DEVICE ADDRESS AND NOT A SUBCHANNEL NUMBER, SO IT   XA0001DK         
*  NEEDS ITS OWN NAME: IOSCHNO WOULD READ AS THE OPPOSITE      XA0001DK         
*  OF THE TRUTH.  S370CHID AND S370ECSW ALREADY SERVE THE      XA0001DK         
*  OTHER TWO GUEST-PSA SITES CORRECTLY.                        XA0001DK         
G370TIO  EQU   IOSSID+2 -     GUEST S/370 DEVICE ADDRESS       XA0001DK         
./ R 00179000          $ 00179010 010                                           
IOINTPRM DS    1F -           ESA/390 IO INTERRUPT PARAMETER   XA0001DK         
         DS    10F -          RESERVED FOR HARDWARE USE        XA0001DK         
./ R 00242490          $ 00242500 010                                           
*  CR0 BITS 8-12 ARE THE TRANSLATION FORMAT. S/370 PUT PAGE    XA0001DK         
*  SIZE IN 8-9 AND SEGMENT SIZE IN 11-12; ESA/390 REQUIRES     XA0001DK         
*  THE SINGLE PATTERN X'00B00000' -- 1 MB SEGMENTS, 4 KB       XA0001DK         
*  PAGES. CE'S X'81800CC0' GIVES X'00800000', WHICH IS 64 KB   XA0001DK         
*  SEGMENTS, AND LRA TAKES A TRANSLATION-SPECIFICATION         XA0001DK         
*  EXCEPTION BEFORE IT READS ANY TABLE. I-152.                 XA0001DK         
CPCREG0  DC    X'81B00CC0' CP ARCH CONTROL AND EXTERNAL MASK   XA0001DK         
./ R 00243000          $ 00243010 010                                           
*  WAS DC F'0' -- CP ASSIST AND VMA MASK. ON ESA/390 CR6 IS    XA0001DK         
*  THE I/O INTERRUPTION SUBCLASS MASK AND ZERO PRESENTS        XA0001DK         
*  NOTHING. ALL EIGHT SUBCLASSES ENABLED; SUBCHANNELS DEFAULT  XA0001DK         
*  TO ISC 0. I-71.                                             XA0001DK         
*  DS 0F BECAUSE LCTL TAKES A SPECIFICATION EXCEPTION ON A     XA0001DK         
*  MISALIGNED OPERAND AND DC X DOES NOT ALIGN. THE OLD DC F    XA0001DK         
*  ALIGNED IMPLICITLY; THIS SAYS IT.                           XA0001DK         
CPCREG6  DS    0F             FULLWORD ALIGNED                 XA0001DK         
         DC    X'FF000000'    CR6 -- IO SUBCLASS MASK          XA0001DK         
./ R 00255600          $ 00255610 010                                           
*  AMODE 31 STUB FOR THE TRANS MACRO. DOCS/34-AMODE31.         XA0001DK         
ATRL31   DC    X'80',AL3(TRL31) 31-BIT ENTRY, FOR BASSM        XA0001DK         
TRL31    LR    R2,R1          24-BIT GUEST: THE ADDRESS IS     XA0001DK         
         N     R2,XRIGHT24    BITS 8-31, WHATEVER BYTE 0 IS    XA0001DK         
         LRA   R2,0(0,R2)     TRANSLATE, IN AMODE 31           XA0001DK         
         BSM   0,R15          BACK TO THE CALLER'S MODE        XA0001DK         
         DS    0F -           RESERVED (WAS 5F)                XA0001DK         
         DS    1F -           RESERVED (WAS 5F)                XA0001DK         
